---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Container from '../components/ui/Container.astro';
import Term from '../components/mdx/Term';
import ThreeLightQuickSim from '../components/checker/ThreeLightQuickSim';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="3-Light Spot Signal Checker & Position Sizing Calculator"
  description="Learn how to copy 5 simple numbers from your Gate.com spot screen into the 3-Light checklist and split your budget safely."
>
  <section class="checker-page">
    <Container size="xl">
      <!-- Friendly Header -->
      <div class="surface-card checker-hero">
        <div class="checker-header">
          <div>
            <span class="status-pill status-pill--info">
              Beginner Safety Checklist · Spot 4H / 1D
            </span>
            <h1 style="margin-top: 8px; margin-bottom: 6px;">
              Spot Signal Checker &amp; Position-Sizing Ladder
            </h1>
            <p class="checker-header__subline">
              Instead of guessing whether to buy or panic-sell on Gate.com, check three simple
              traffic lights and divide your budget into safe, pre-planned steps.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a href="/learn/01-how-a-chart-is-built" class="btn-secondary">
            Need help finding these numbers? View Screen Map &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="analogy-callout" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
          <div class="analogy-callout__header">
            Everyday Analogy: The 3-Light Street Crossing Rule
          </div>
          <p>
            Imagine crossing a busy 3-lane road. You do not run across just because Lane 1 is clear.
            You wait until <strong>all 3 lanes are clear at the same time</strong>: (1) The coin is
            cheaper than its recent 30-bar average, (2) Sellers are tired on the RSI meter, and (3)
            Real buyers are waiting with cash in the Order Book.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Interactive 3-Light Engine Simulator -->
      <ThreeLightQuickSim client:load />

      <!-- Step-by-Step Guide with Concrete Examples -->
      <div class="checker-grid">
        <!-- Left Card: The 5 Numbers You Read from Gate.com -->
        <article class="surface-card">
          <h2>Step 1: Where to Find the 5 Numbers on Gate.com</h2>
          <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: var(--font-size-sm); margin-bottom: 16px;">
            Open your exchange on the <strong>Spot</strong> tab and click the{' '}
            <Term client:visible id="timeframe">
              4H or 1D
            </Term>{' '}
            button above the chart. Here is every number you need, with a real Solana (SOL/USDT)
            example:
          </p>

          <div class="example-list">
            <div class="example-item">
              <div class="example-item__top">
                <strong>1. Current Price &amp; MA30 Average (Light 1)</strong>
                <span class="status-pill status-pill--positive num">
                  Example: $128.18 vs $129.07
                </span>
              </div>
              <p>
                Compare the big price at the top-left (<code class="num">128.18</code>) against the{' '}
                <Term client:visible id="ma30">
                  MA30
                </Term>{' '}
                number printed at the top of the chart (<code class="num">129.07</code>). Because{' '}
                <code class="num">$128.18</code> is below <code class="num">$129.07</code>, the coin
                is on discount (<strong>Light 1 ON</strong>).
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="example-item">
              <div class="example-item__top">
                <strong>2. RSI Momentum Meter (Light 2)</strong>
                <span class="status-pill status-pill--positive num">
                  Example: RSI = 32.57 (&le; 36)
                </span>
              </div>
              <p>
                Look at the{' '}
                <Term client:visible id="rsi">
                  RSI
                </Term>{' '}
                sub-chart at the bottom of your screen (0 to 100). When RSI is{' '}
                <strong>36 or lower</strong>, recent selling is exhausted (
                <strong>Light 2 ON</strong>).
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="example-item">
              <div class="example-item__top">
                <strong>3. Order Book Buyer % (Light 3)</strong>
                <span class="status-pill status-pill--positive num">
                  Example: 41.58% Buyers (&ge; 40%)
                </span>
              </div>
              <p>
                Look at the green vs red tug-of-war bar in the{' '}
                <Term client:visible id="order-book">
                  Order Book
                </Term>
                . When Green Buyers make up <strong>at least 40%</strong>, real demand is waiting
                below (<strong>Light 3 ON</strong>).
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="example-item">
              <div class="example-item__top">
                <strong>4. Nearest Support Floors &amp; Ceiling</strong>
                <span class="status-pill status-pill--info num">
                  Floors: $128 / $126.64 / $124.50
                </span>
              </div>
              <p>
                Look left on the chart to see where red drops previously bounced up (your{' '}
                <Term client:visible id="support">
                  Support Floors
                </Term>
                ) and where green rallies stalled (
                <Term client:visible id="resistance">
                  Resistance Ceiling
                </Term>{' '}
                at <code class="num">$135.00</code>).
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Right Card: What the 4 Result Badges Tell You to Do -->
        <article class="surface-card">
          <h2>Step 2: What Each Result Badge Means in Plain English</h2>
          <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: var(--font-size-sm); margin-bottom: 16px;">
            Once you enter those numbers, you get one of four calm, unmistakable action plans:
          </p>

          <div class="example-list">
            <div class="example-item">
              <div class="example-item__top">
                <span class="status-pill status-pill--positive">
                  &#10003; Buy Zone: Consider Split Entry
                </span>
                <span class="num" style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700;">
                  All 3 Lights ON
                </span>
              </div>
              <p>
                <strong>What to do:</strong> Place your first small{' '}
                <Term client:visible id="limit-order">
                  Limit Buy
                </Term>{' '}
                for only <strong>13% of your budget</strong> ($30 out of $233.77) at Support Floor
                1, place 21% ($50) at Floor 2, 30% ($70) at Floor 3, and keep{' '}
                <strong>36% ($83.77)</strong> untouched in cash.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="example-item">
              <div class="example-item__top">
                <span class="status-pill status-pill--warning">&bull; Wait: Hold Your Cash</span>
                <span class="num" style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700;">
                  1 or 2 Lights OFF
                </span>
              </div>
              <p>
                <strong>Real example (ETH):</strong> ETH dropped below MA30 and had RSI 35,{' '}
                <em>but</em> Order Book Buyers were only <strong>22%</strong> (Light 3 OFF). Waiting
                protected your cash from catching a falling knife.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="example-item">
              <div class="example-item__top">
                <span class="status-pill status-pill--info">
                  &uarr; Take Profit: Sell Some or All
                </span>
                <span class="num" style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700;">
                  Holding Near Ceiling
                </span>
              </div>
              <p>
                <strong>What to do:</strong> When price reaches your Resistance Ceiling ($135.00) or
                RSI overheats above 70, place a Limit Sell to lock in gains calmly instead of
                getting greedy.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="example-item">
              <div class="example-item__top">
                <span class="status-pill status-pill--negative">
                  ! Plan Broken: Consider Exiting
                </span>
                <span class="num" style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700;">
                  Below Stop-Loss
                </span>
              </div>
              <p>
                <strong>What to do:</strong> If a 4H candle closes more than 2% below your lowest
                support floor ($122.01), your reason for buying is broken. Follow your{' '}
                <Term client:visible id="stop-loss">
                  Stop-Loss
                </Term>{' '}
                and protect your cash.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .checker-page {
    padding-block: var(--space-8) var(--space-16);
  }

  .checker-hero {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .checker-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }

  .checker-header__subline {
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 88ch;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .checker-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-5);
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .checker-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .surface-card h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .example-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .example-item {
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background-color: var(--color-bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
  }

  .example-item__top {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .example-item p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-main);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>
